public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RelativeProjClosedSubspaceEquations
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RelativeProjPoint.ChartReadingRestrict
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.SmallEtaleAffineRefinement
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.EtaleLocal.FromLocalAtSource

/-!
# The graded ideal of a closed subspace of the constructed relative Proj, read on étale charts

Let `π : P = Proj_X(𝒜) ⟶ X` be the relative homogeneous spectrum of Situation 0849 constructed in
Stacks 084A–084B and `i : Z ⟶ P` a closed immersion.  Over an étale chart `V = (T, v)` of `X` the
fibre `Z_V ⊆ Proj_T(v^*𝒜)` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.fibreClosedImmersion`)
has its equations (Tag 0801), and a section `a` of `𝒜_d` over `V` is read as a global section of
`(v^*𝒜)_d` by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartOpenReading`.  This file proves the two properties of
"being an equation" on which the chart-by-chart description of the degree `d` part `ℐ_d ⊆ 𝒜_d` of
the graded ideal of `Z` of Stacks 085L rests: equations restrict to equations along morphisms of
étale charts, and being an equation is local on the small étale site of `X`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.exists_isPullback_fibreClosedImmersion_of_eq`:
  along a morphism of charts the fibres of `Z` form the base-change square of Stacks 084B (3),
  for an arbitrary spelling `f'` of the restricted point.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.twistEquationSection_eq_zero_of_pointRestrict`
  and `.twistEquationSection_chartOpenReading_restrict`: **equations restrict to equations** along
  the restriction datum, and along morphisms of étale charts.
* `RelativeProjSituation.twistEquationSection_eq_zero_of_pointRestrict_cover`: being an
  equation descends along a jointly surjective family of flat affine test objects.
* `RelativeProjSituation.twistEquationSection_chartOpenReading_of_mem_topology`: **being an
  equation is local on the small étale site** of `X`, over affine charts.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.IsChartEquation` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.chartIdeal`: **the degree `d` part `ℐ_d ⊆ 𝒜_d` of
  the graded ideal of `Z`**, as a submodule of `𝒜_d` on the small étale site of `X` (for `π`
  quasi-compact): the sections whose readings over the affine étale charts above are equations of
  the fibres of `Z` there; its sections over an affine chart are equations
  (`IsChartEquation.twistEquationSection_eq_zero`).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 085L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/085L)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 084B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/084B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0801](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0801)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj
